# Flok multi-agent

Lead agent owns planning, commits, and PRs. Parallelize only independent streams. Prefer existing skills `multi-agent` / `swarm` for orchestration patterns — do not paste their full text here.

## Model routing

**Default child agents = Composer.** Maximize parallel Composer workers for throughput. Expensive models are thin gates only — never bulk coding.

### Default (Composer workers)

| Role / task | `subagent_type` | `model` | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Lead routine implementation | parent | `inherit` | Composer parent plans, commits, synthesizes. |
| Broad map / scout | `explore` | `composer-2.5-fast` | Fast repo discovery. |
| Backend / API / tokens / Grade | `backend-engineer` | `inherit` | Composer — parent or spawned child. |
| Frontend / OG / tiles | `frontend-engineer` | `inherit` | Composer — parent or spawned child. |
| Shell / mechanical ops | `shell` | `composer-2.5-fast` | Terminal and mechanical work. |
| Large-volume repo analysis | `repo-analyst` | `inherit` | Only if huge; prefer `inherit` for coherence. |
| Parallel file-split workers | any | `inherit` | Spawn 2–4 Composer children when files do not overlap. |

### Expensive gates only

| Role / task | `subagent_type` | `model` | When |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ambiguous design / Grade API | `architect` | `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` | Design is ambiguous; skip for mechanical work. |
| Security: secrets / OG / auth | `security-auditor` | `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` | Secrets, auth, OG, high risk only. |
| Verifier after wave | `verifier` | `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` | After non-trivial work; **one** verifier, not many. |
| High-risk adversarial challenge | `red-team` | `claude-fable-5-thinking-high` | High-impact only. |
| External docs and prior art | `researcher` | `gemini-3.1-pro` | External docs only. |

Do not spawn Opus, Sol, Fable, or Kimi for routine explore/implement — that kills throughput. Verifier must differ from implementer model family.

## Parallelism rules

- Prefer **2–4 Composer Task children in parallel** when file ownership does not overlap.
- One ownership matrix per wave; **no two children edit the same file**.
- Lead synthesizes parallel output; **only then** run ONE verifier (and security-auditor if needed).
- Do not spawn multiple verifiers or architects for the same wave.

## Wave recipes

1. **Grok debt / harness fix:** `explore` (`composer-2.5-fast`) → implement on parent (`inherit`) → `security-auditor` (`claude-opus-5-thinking-high`) if trust-boundary touched → **one** `verifier` (`claude-opus-5-thinking-high`).
2. **S1 Grade:** short `architect` (`claude-opus-5-thinking-high`) brief if design ambiguous → `backend-engineer` (`inherit`) ∥ `frontend-engineer` (`inherit`) → **one** `verifier` (`claude-opus-5-thinking-high`) → `flok-ship`.

## Ownership

- One file-ownership matrix per parallel wave; no two workers edit the same file.
- Subagent prompts are self-contained: objective, files, constraints, acceptance criteria.
- Never merge a PR without explicit user approval.
- Do not treat BRAIN or `reference/spx402/` as the product spec.
- Hire Hall stays closed until SPX402 `OC_*` (S2). See `AGENTS.md`.
